(:id "port/python/vt/text-form/json" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonScan" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonScanPolicy" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonWideCorpus" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonGeneratedWriterMatchesWalk" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonConformanceDriver" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonFieldMatchNegativeControl" "make/python-json.mk: python-json" "make/python-json.mk: python-json-negative-control") :tested-revision "7a7d4071d16de05f2cbeb759788186775ae7f192" :note "2026-11-17: the JSON reader (a port of the engine's scanner and descriptor conversion) and the deterministic writer, for every table and field kind the leg carries. The TestPythonJson group passed under both pinned interpreters, CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 on macOS arm64 at this revision: JSONTestSuite policy rows, duplicate keys, lone surrogates and non-finite numbers refused, every readable input written back byte-identical, and the json-read, json-write, json-hostile, report and write-refusal-json conformance surfaces. Integers wider than 32 bits and the 64- and 128-bit fixed-point kinds read and write as JSON strings; a bare number token there refuses kind_mismatch at a plain field, array element, optional, union arm, union array, map value and enum-keyed slot (testdata/wire/json-integers MANIFEST.tsv and NUMBER-TOKEN.tsv), 32-bit and narrower integers read their number, and the writer refuses an out-of-range wide value. Planting a number-token acceptance in the runtime reader, a duplicate-key acceptance in the scanner, or dropping the writer's range check turns the group red by name; the field-key negative control is python-json-negative-control.")
(:id "port/python/vt/text-form-variable" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonSharedNodes" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonPointerArraysAgainstEngine" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonOptionalMapsAgainstEngine" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonUnionArray" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonArrayRoot" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonBlobRef" "internal/codegen/pythontable/json_scan_test.go: TestPythonJsonFieldMatchNegativeControl" "make/python-json.mk: python-json" "make/python-json.mk: python-json-negative-control") :tested-revision "7a7d4071d16de05f2cbeb759788186775ae7f192" :note "2026-11-17: the JSON text form over the variable class: shared nodes and their labels, pointers and pointer arrays, unbounded arrays, maps and optional maps, unions and union arrays, blobs, blob references and array roots, checked against the engine's reader and writer. The TestPythonJson group passed under both pinned interpreters, CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 on macOS arm64 at this revision; the field-key negative control is python-json-negative-control.")
